{
  "id": "Math10_Q3_M02",
  "title": "Factorials",
  "topic": "Permutation",
  "description": "",
  "lesson": [
    {
      "heading": "What is Factorial?",
      "text": "A factorial is the product of all positive integers up to a given number and denoted by that integer (n) and an exclamation point. Thus n! isread as n factorial. It is used in permutations and combinations."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Example of Factorial Calculation",
      "bullets": [
        "5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120",
        "4! = 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 24",
        "3! = 3 x 2 x 1 = 6",
        "2! = 2 x 1 = 2",
        "1! = 1",
        "0! = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Example 1: \nRewrite the following factorials.",
      "bullets": [
        "A. 12! with a factor 9! \n \t \t 12! = 12 x 11 x 10 x 9!",
        "B. 15! with a factor 13! \n \t \t 15! = 15 x 14 x 13!",
        "C. 10! with a factor 5! \n \t \t 10! = 10 x 9 x 8 x 7 x 6 x 5!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Example 2: \nEvaluate each factorial notation.",
      "bullets": [
        "A. 6! = 6 x 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 720",
        "B. (6 - 2)! = 4! = 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 24",
        "C. 7!/4!+3! = 7 x 6 x 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 / (4 x 3 x 2 x 1)+(3 x 2 x 1) = 5,040/24+6 = 168"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Example 3: \nSolve for x.",
      "bullets": [
        "A. x = 8! = 8 x 7 x 6 x 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 \n \t \t x = 40,320",
        "B. x + 3! = 6! \n \t \t x = 6! - 3! \n \t \t x = (6 x 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1) - (3 x 2 x 1) \n \t \t x = 720 - 6 \n \t \t x = 714",
        "C. 3x = 4!/2! \n \t \t 3x = 4 x 3 x 2 x 1/2 x 1 \n \t \t x = (6 x 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1) - (3 x 2 x 1) \n \t \t x = 720 - 6 \n \t \t x = 714"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
